A||||2||Standard||I think I killed a firebird...||||6||
Z||000000||Standard||07-24-2001||02:48 AM||||Cruising home on the freeway tonight, doing 55.  Late 80's Firebird merges in behind me.  I'm kinda itchin' for a race but just decide to wait and see if he makes a move.. he stays behind me for awhile the switches lanes and passes me at about 60 or so.  I wait 'till he's a few carlengths ahead, then drop it into 2nd.  Quick redline, 3rd gear and I fly by him.  Coast back down to 55 and leave it in 3rd, waiting for him to get next to me.  As soon as he's right beside me I hammer it.  Even up to 70mph and then I just walk away from him.  I don't know if he shut down or what...  Wait for him to get next to me again but they just cruise by at about 65 without looking over.  hehe  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_pic_full.jpg">        <BR>1988 Quad 4 Coupe 5 speed<P><FONT SIZE="1">1986 GT 5 speed, 1984 SC Auto<BR><FONT COLOR="red">AOL: LastMinuteBastrd  AIM: SavedbyJebus</FONT></FONT>||||reg||6
Z||000001||rodmcneill||07-24-2001||03:12 AM||||Standard, give us a test report on your new ride. I had been looking at that one when it first went up for sale. How is the handling, brakes etc? Had all the bugs been worked out especially in the wiring? It looked like he put a lot of labor and money in that one.||||reg||5
Z||000002||Standard||07-24-2001||02:18 PM||||Handles like a slot car and will stop on a dime  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  The only "bug" I'm having right now is the sensor for the temp gauge is grounding out somewhere and making the gauge twitch all over, but that's just annoying.  I've put over 2,000 miles on it since I got it.  Biggest problem was the throttle would slightly stick, but that was just a broken throttle pedal, took a whole 20 minutes to fix.  <P>Cruise works, AC works, all the gauges work.  I've been getting ~30 mpg with alot of city driving.  The biggest issue is the quad developes alot of heat, and with the exhaust manifold right by the trunk wall things tend to get very hot back there.  So I'm thinking about doing a Skitime-style decklid vent, or a 'stang hoodscoop.<P>Paul did put a lot of work into this car!  Very clean install.  I'm lovin' every minute of it!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
